nts involved a male driver, 56% of the accidents involved speeding, and in 10% of the accidents the driver was female and was not speeding.","position":{"start":{"line":100,"column":1},"end":{"line":100,"column":1}},"key":"FVAhBgSJuV"}],"key":"XJUZgXhm8R"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":102,"column":1},"end":{"line":102,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"(We’ll use M for an accident involving a male driver, F [= not M] for a female driver, and G for an accident involving speeding.)","position":{"start":{"line":102,"column":1},"end":{"line":102,"column":1}},"key":"VxTaCt31UT"}],"key":"O1XrEEmRRc"},{"type":"anywidget","esm":"/textbook/build/quiz-widget-ab552a073177c801fc08fc2e7e8860b3.mjs","model":{"question":"What is P(F and G)—the probability that an accident involved a female driver who was speeding?","choices":[{"correct":true,"text":"0.03","feedback":"Correct! P(F) = 0.13 and P(F and not G) = 0.10, so P(F and G) = $0.13 - 0.10 = 0.03$."},{"correct":false,"text":"0.13","feedback":"0.13 is P(F), the whole row; subtract the not-speeding part."},{"correct":false,"text":"0.10","feedback":"0.10 is P(F and not G), given in the problem."}],"multi":false,"hint":"P(F) = $1 - 0.87 = 0.13$, and the F row splits into \"speeding\" and \"not speeding.\"","explanation":""},"key":"Z0O1l0pvu3"},{"type":"anywidget","esm":"/textbook/build/quiz-widget-ab552a073177c801fc08fc2e7e8860b3.mjs","model":{"question":"What is P(M and G)—the probability that an accident involved a male driver who was speeding?","choices":[{"correct":true,"text":"0.53","feedback":"Correct! P(M and G) = P(G) - P(F and G) = $0.56 - 0.03 = 0.53$."},{"correct":false,"text":"0.56","feedback":"0.56 is the total probability of speeding accidents, including female drivers."},{"correct":false,"text":"0.49","feedback":"$0.87 \\times 0.56$ assumes M and G are independent, which we have no reason to believe here—use the table instead."}],"multi":false,"hint":"The G column totals 0.56, and you